    cross: ["Isaiah 45:23 — “to me every knee shall bow” (quoted by Paul)", "Luke 10:17–20 — “even the demons are subject to us in your name”", "Acts 3:6; 16:18 — healing and deliverance in Jesus' name", "Acts 19:13–16 — the sons of Sceva: the name is not a formula", "John 14:13–14 — asking in his name", "Mark 16:17"],
    background: "In the ancient world, a “name” stood for a person's character and authority. Acting “in the name of” someone meant acting as their authorized representative, much like an ambassador or agent. Philippians 2:10–11 applies Isaiah 45:23, a passage about YHWH alone, to Jesus. Acts 19:13–16 (the sons of Sceva) is a sober warning that the name is not a magic incantation, which matches the speaker's own point.",
