    cross: ["2 Chronicles 20:12, 15, 17 — “the battle is not yours but God's”", "Joshua 6 — Jericho falls at the shout", "Psalm 149:6 — praises in their mouths, swords in their hands", "Acts 16:25–26 — Paul and Silas sing at midnight", "Psalm 22:3 — God enthroned on the praises of Israel", "Hebrews 13:15 — the sacrifice of praise"],
    background: "The armies were Moab, Ammon and men from Mount Seir/Meunites (2 Chr 20:1, 10, 22). Before the worship came prayer and fasting: Jehoshaphat proclaimed a fast (v.3) and prayed, “we do not know what to do, but our eyes are on you” (v.12). A prophetic word followed (v.15–17). Praise came out of that dependence and obedience. The song in v.21, “his steadfast love (<em>ḥesed</em>) endures forever,” is the refrain of Psalm 136.",
