    cross: ["John 8:44 — the father of lies", "Proverbs 14:15 — the simple believe everything", "Ephesians 4:15 — speaking the truth in love", "Psalm 46:10 — be still, and know"],
    background: "<b>The Blood vs. the algorithm of accusation:</b> Feeds that reward shame and outrage echo “the accuser.” The finished work of Christ is your answer to every comparison, every “you're not enough,” and every digital pile-on.<br><br><b>The Name vs. counterfeit authority:</b> AI can sound authoritative while being wrong. Authority belongs to Christ, so test every voice, whether human, algorithmic or “spiritual,” against Scripture (1 John 4:1).<br><br><b>Praise vs. infinite distraction:</b> Attention is the new battleground. Choosing worship over the scroll is a real act of warfare: it puts God, not the feed, in the center.<br><br><b>Fight people? No:</b> Online, the enemy loves turning people into targets. The sermon's line “your enemy is not your spouse… your boss” applies to comment sections too.",
